  "summary": "The task is not complete. I wrote no scene, because `@aura3d/engine` is not installed in this sandbox. `node_modules/@aura3d/` is an empty directory, and `read_file` on `@aura3d/engine/package.json`, `dist/index.d.ts` and `@aura3d/assets/package.json` all fail with \"is not a file\". A probe file with `import { material } from \"@aura3d/engine\"` fails `typecheck` with TS2307 (cannot find module). The docs describe `material.physical`, `material.proceduralTextures` and `environments.*`, but I couldn't see the types for the glass transmission/IOR, anisotropy or sheen fields. Code written without the package could not be typechecked or built. I did not substitute a hand-written WebGL renderer, because the assignment requires Aura3D and that would be a different deliverable. `src/main.ts` is a placeholder that only contains `export {}`. The sandbox needs a working install of `@aura3d/engine@5.0.2`. My plan for the scene was these Aura3D parts:\n- `environments.studio`/`metalStudio`/`glassStudio` for the reflections.\n- A big key light (`lights.rect`/`softbox` or a directional), a dim fill and a rim light.\n- A `primitives.plane` or lathe floor that curves up into the backdrop.\n- `effects.contactShadows`.\n- Three `primitives.sphere` nodes with `material.clearGlass`, `material.brushedMetal` and `material.fabric` plus `proceduralTextures`.\n- An `app.onFrame` loop that drifts the key light's x and updates `window.__TASK_STATE__`.\n- `window.__EVAL_READY__ = true` after `await app.ready()`.",
